.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH push 1  "push " 
.SH NAME
push \- Push a local snippet to the cloud (create or new version)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpush\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR] [\fB\-\-unlisted\fR] [\fB\-\-private\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-registry\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Push a local snippet to the cloud (create or new version)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Push every local snippet and print a summary
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
Make the snippet public
.TP
\fB\-\-unlisted\fR
Make the snippet unlisted
.TP
\fB\-\-private\fR
Make the snippet private (the default for new snippets)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
Version message for the push
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<AS_NAME>\fR
Push under a different remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR \fI<REGISTRY>\fR
Registry base URL (default: `FORGEHUB_REGISTRY` or config)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Local snippet name (omit with \-\-all)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg push ubuntu\-setup \-\-public
  fg push \-\-all
